WEBVTT

00:29.861 --> 00:34.031
(Azure Spring)

00:34.032 --> 00:36.433
(All characters, places, events, etc.. depicted are fictional.)

00:36.434 --> 00:38.970
(Children and animals were filmed under strict guidelines.)

00:46.344 --> 00:47.913
Where did they go this time?

01:06.231 --> 01:07.432
Unbelievable.

01:08.733 --> 01:10.168
Seo An Na, you...

01:22.814 --> 01:28.820
(Episode 3: The Timing)

01:32.757 --> 01:35.493
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

01:44.436 --> 01:46.716
Doing this prevents your goggles from fogging underwater.

01:49.007 --> 01:50.976
Like anti-fog coating?

01:51.610 --> 01:54.179
The sea works around its own clock.

01:55.614 --> 01:57.349
High tide, low tide, and the tidal cycle.

01:58.116 --> 01:59.217
I know that much.

01:59.451 --> 02:02.554
You knew that, yet you went in during the most dangerous time?

02:04.856 --> 02:05.891
I did?

02:07.526 --> 02:08.860
You got swept away instantly...

02:09.528 --> 02:10.862
by the strong current.

02:19.871 --> 02:21.805
The time when the current is weakest...

02:21.806 --> 02:24.166
between the low and the high tide is called the slack tide.

02:25.210 --> 02:26.844
It is the only time, occurring twice a day,

02:26.845 --> 02:29.181
when the sea allows free divers to harvest seafood.

02:30.682 --> 02:32.551
So when is that?

02:34.386 --> 02:35.487
Right now.

02:40.892 --> 02:42.928
You're right. I guess...

02:43.495 --> 02:45.197
it seems rather peaceful.

02:46.264 --> 02:47.432
Let's go in.

02:49.234 --> 02:51.670
The slack tide lasts only three hours at most.

02:59.811 --> 03:00.979
Wait up!

03:04.149 --> 03:05.250
Hey, wait up!

03:05.990 --> 03:07.292
I said, wait for me!

03:37.782 --> 03:39.150
Stand straight. You're heavy.

03:43.288 --> 03:44.389
I'm not that...

03:46.925 --> 03:49.461
Hey! You two jerks!

03:53.498 --> 03:54.533
Baek Su Jeong?

03:55.901 --> 03:58.470
Seo An Na, I'm the idiot...

03:59.738 --> 04:01.106
for trusting you.

04:02.674 --> 04:04.341
You wench!

04:04.342 --> 04:06.211
Hey, you're going to fall!

04:09.748 --> 04:11.683
Stop pretending like you're nice.

04:12.083 --> 04:13.951
What? What are you talking about?

04:13.952 --> 04:16.153
You said you weren't into Duk Hyun!

04:16.154 --> 04:18.656
How can you do this to me?

04:18.657 --> 04:20.424
I'm not!

04:20.425 --> 04:22.661
You said you didn't get what was sexy about him.

04:22.861 --> 04:25.262
What? "Sexy"? You call that guy sexy?

04:25.263 --> 04:26.531
You!

04:28.500 --> 04:29.501
Hey!

04:30.135 --> 04:31.169
You two...

04:40.745 --> 04:43.148
Duk Hyun, do me first.

04:43.682 --> 04:45.550
I'm more badly hurt.

04:48.920 --> 04:50.255
Please settle this on your own.

04:52.123 --> 04:53.458
Where are you going?

04:53.792 --> 04:55.459
I have an ouchie right here.

04:55.460 --> 04:57.394
You need to put some medicine on me.

04:57.395 --> 04:58.896
Duk Hyun!

04:58.897 --> 05:01.299
Hey, I got you.

05:03.235 --> 05:04.336
Come closer.

05:07.939 --> 05:09.374
Stay still.

05:09.941 --> 05:10.942
Jeez.

05:11.476 --> 05:14.246
Even if you do this, I still won't let it slide.

05:15.547 --> 05:18.016
It's nothing like what you're imagining.

05:18.450 --> 05:19.584
It so is.

05:19.918 --> 05:22.921
You two harvest seafood together, eat together,

05:23.154 --> 05:24.555
work out together,

05:24.556 --> 05:27.791
touch each other, and feel each other up!

05:27.792 --> 05:28.793
Hey!

05:28.927 --> 05:30.828
I like men who aren't tanned...

05:30.829 --> 05:32.097
and are sweet.

05:32.664 --> 05:33.899
Exactly.

05:34.332 --> 05:38.303
Duk Hyun has such a sweet and handsome face!

05:39.738 --> 05:41.239
Su Jeong, please.

05:44.342 --> 05:46.845
You and I aren't besties anymore.

05:47.612 --> 05:49.714
This is war, you traitor.

05:50.215 --> 05:53.451
Don't ever act friendly and call me Su Jeong without my surname,

05:54.085 --> 05:56.021
Seo An Na.

06:01.159 --> 06:03.061
We weren't best friends to start with.

06:05.030 --> 06:06.364
That was a decade ago.

06:29.654 --> 06:30.934
Aren't you going out to harvest?

06:31.456 --> 06:33.190
I already told you.

06:33.191 --> 06:35.427
The slack tide only lasts three hours at most.

06:37.395 --> 06:38.396
Also,

06:39.197 --> 06:41.466
you'd better not touch the water for a while.

06:45.437 --> 06:46.605
You know what?

06:47.539 --> 06:48.907
You're rude,

06:49.708 --> 06:51.109
but you're also oddly sweet.

06:51.977 --> 06:52.978
Impossible.

06:58.416 --> 07:00.951
Even if you didn't get to harvest, wash the suit before drying it.

07:00.952 --> 07:03.112
Even a little bit of salt can easily corrode the suit.

07:04.623 --> 07:05.991
Yeah, yeah.

07:07.559 --> 07:08.927
I shouldn't have said anything.

07:09.895 --> 07:10.896
Also,

07:11.329 --> 07:13.009
clear the air between you and your friend.

07:14.699 --> 07:15.699
Why?

07:15.700 --> 07:17.334
Are you scared you'll be known around the island...

07:17.335 --> 07:18.937
as a player who's toying with two girls?

07:21.239 --> 07:23.519
Just like the sea, there's a right timing between people.

07:24.809 --> 07:26.129
If you miss it, you won't find...

07:27.712 --> 07:29.414
another chance for a very long time.

07:34.920 --> 07:36.288
I shouldn't have been so nosy.

07:44.029 --> 07:45.030
What was that?

07:46.097 --> 07:47.165
Trying to act all cool.

07:52.070 --> 07:54.939
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

07:54.940 --> 07:57.542
Well, I guess I had always pushed everything aside...

07:58.310 --> 07:59.744
except for swimming.

08:01.980 --> 08:04.015
I told you to stop sending me food.

08:04.449 --> 08:06.051
I can't even finish these.

08:06.551 --> 08:08.653
I feed myself all right.

08:09.054 --> 08:10.789
Stop worrying about me.

08:12.324 --> 08:13.859
No, I said I'm fine!

08:15.727 --> 08:17.362
"I'm busy now, so maybe later."

08:21.333 --> 08:23.134
"I can always do it next time,"

08:23.869 --> 08:24.903
"so maybe later."

08:44.656 --> 08:47.592
You little brat. You didn't even touch these.

08:50.095 --> 08:51.630
Do you know how hurtful this is?

08:55.033 --> 08:56.701
I kept pushing everything back,

08:57.135 --> 08:58.170
and in the end,

08:59.137 --> 09:00.272
I ended up hurting her.

09:15.954 --> 09:17.155
I missed...

09:18.623 --> 09:19.658
the important timing.

09:20.792 --> 09:23.628
(Parang-ri Haenyeo Cho Mi Hyeon)

09:28.300 --> 09:29.367
How am I...

09:30.535 --> 09:32.270
supposed to clear the air between us?

10:12.143 --> 10:13.278
Are these red beans?

10:14.312 --> 10:15.981
Jeez, I have no idea.

10:17.048 --> 10:19.518
After all, this isn't the supermarket.

10:20.151 --> 10:21.271
I doubt there are red beans.

10:21.920 --> 10:23.622
Even if there were, it's not yet time.

10:27.425 --> 10:29.665
Red beans are sown in the summer and reaped in the fall.

10:32.664 --> 10:34.032
Thanks for the info.

10:40.172 --> 10:42.140
What? You said there weren't any.

10:42.474 --> 10:44.275
I just said it wasn't harvest season yet.

10:44.276 --> 10:45.343
These are from last year.

10:47.746 --> 10:48.880
Thanks.

11:34.392 --> 11:35.393
Hey.

11:36.328 --> 11:37.329
Hey!

11:39.030 --> 11:41.766
Why don't you help me, so that I don't miss the timing?

11:48.340 --> 11:49.908
Go. Come on.

11:55.213 --> 11:56.214
Open it.

12:04.523 --> 12:05.523
Come on.

12:05.524 --> 12:06.558
Stir it like this.

12:33.084 --> 12:34.653
Keep going.

13:08.453 --> 13:11.356
When you think about it, timing is everything.

13:19.865 --> 13:20.932
In harvesting seafood,

13:21.700 --> 13:22.701
relationships,

13:23.935 --> 13:24.936
and making dough.

13:26.004 --> 13:27.539
It's all about timing.

13:57.369 --> 13:58.569
How long do I have to do this?

13:59.070 --> 14:00.338
Bring it over here.

15:06.738 --> 15:07.772
Look at this.

15:48.713 --> 15:50.148
A long wait and perfect timing...

15:50.916 --> 15:52.317
are required even when you make...

15:53.218 --> 15:54.953
these simple honey donuts.

15:56.188 --> 15:58.523
Everything comes down to timing.

16:05.230 --> 16:06.231
Try one.

16:22.781 --> 16:26.083
Come to Parang Elementary School. Immediately. Right now.

16:26.084 --> 16:27.586
(Seo An Na)

16:38.897 --> 16:40.098
Jeez, that girl.

16:40.465 --> 16:42.200
Why did she call me out all the way here?

16:57.482 --> 16:58.783
What the heck, Su Jeong?

16:59.150 --> 17:01.086
You called me here, yet you show up late.

17:02.387 --> 17:04.489
Here. Have it on your way to Seoul.

17:11.029 --> 17:12.597
Gosh, honey donuts?

17:13.098 --> 17:15.858
I got sick of these here. Are you telling me to eat it in Seoul, too?

17:16.735 --> 17:19.905
You didn't even tell me you were moving to Seoul,

17:20.939 --> 17:23.074
so I didn't have time to prepare a present.

17:32.117 --> 17:34.986
What is this? Do you think some donuts are enough to call it even?

17:35.720 --> 17:37.222
These aren't just some donuts.

17:37.856 --> 17:39.057
You once said...

17:39.558 --> 17:42.627
that honey donuts are a way of saying, "Have a safe trip."

17:49.334 --> 17:51.036
I told you to have them on your way there.

17:52.737 --> 17:55.407
It doesn't matter where you eat these.

17:55.640 --> 17:57.909
It does! My dad said...

17:58.476 --> 18:01.646
honey donuts are made with a lot of syrup, so they last long.

18:02.314 --> 18:04.582
That's why my mom always makes them...

18:04.583 --> 18:06.451
for my dad before he goes out to sea.

18:08.687 --> 18:10.407
It's her way of saying, "Have a safe trip."

18:25.003 --> 18:27.639
So these aren't just any honey donuts.

18:28.773 --> 18:29.875
They're my way of saying,

18:32.477 --> 18:33.545
"Thanks to you."

18:34.646 --> 18:37.148
"I had a great trip, Baek Su Jeong."

18:39.351 --> 18:41.019
Whatever, girl.

18:43.588 --> 18:45.657
Wait, are you crying?

18:47.926 --> 18:50.629
I'm not crying. I just got thirsty.

18:55.667 --> 18:57.569
Hey, did you just laugh at me?

18:57.802 --> 18:59.704
Yes, I did. So what?

19:02.440 --> 19:04.009
So? Do you like it?

19:04.609 --> 19:05.769
I've never made these before.

19:09.014 --> 19:10.115
These are really...

19:13.251 --> 19:14.252
delicious.

19:18.056 --> 19:20.258
Doing this won't make me give up on Duk Hyun for you.

19:20.525 --> 19:21.993
Don't you dare try to steal him.

19:23.061 --> 19:26.097
- Gosh, I'm not interested! - Aren't you lying?

19:28.466 --> 19:29.834
- What the heck? - It's raining.

19:29.835 --> 19:30.836
It's raining!

19:32.237 --> 19:34.639
The sky is so clear. Why is it suddenly raining?

19:35.207 --> 19:36.274
Run!

19:58.163 --> 20:00.264
A typhoon is coming. We can't go harvesting for a while.

20:00.265 --> 20:01.266
What?

20:04.302 --> 20:05.702
What are you doing? Give me a hand.

20:09.274 --> 20:11.710
There's a time for everything.

20:14.579 --> 20:17.648
A typhoon is moving rapidly northward.

20:17.649 --> 20:21.185
Heavy rain is expected across the country for the time being,

20:21.186 --> 20:24.655
with localized downpours exceeding 80mm per hour...

20:24.656 --> 20:27.825
along the southern coast, raising concerns about possible damage.

20:27.826 --> 20:31.963
The weather is expected to be at its worst from tonight through dawn.

20:33.732 --> 20:34.900
- Darn it. - My gosh!

20:36.468 --> 20:37.536
Come on!

20:39.437 --> 20:41.038
What are you doing? Stick it on!

20:41.039 --> 20:42.374
Give me a moment, will you?

20:44.276 --> 20:45.577
Hold this, please!

21:01.359 --> 21:02.894
While you wait for the right timing,

21:03.295 --> 21:05.030
you may face a huge ordeal...

21:05.730 --> 21:06.998
and may even fall apart.

21:16.675 --> 21:18.176
But even the fiercest storms...

21:19.144 --> 21:20.345
eventually pass.

21:37.329 --> 21:38.396
Shall we go today?

21:42.767 --> 21:43.768
To harvest seafood.

22:04.356 --> 22:07.292
When the storm passes and the impurities are gone,

22:11.830 --> 22:13.932
the sea is ready to give new life.

22:19.471 --> 22:22.440
Just like that, the timing comes.

22:27.479 --> 22:28.480
Let's go.

22:42.294 --> 22:43.595
Wait!

22:46.498 --> 22:47.899
No one should go out to dive...

22:50.468 --> 22:51.536
on an empty stomach.

22:53.438 --> 22:55.040
I do it on an empty stomach.

22:56.060 --> 22:58.162
Oh, my.

22:58.502 --> 23:02.106
Then you can eat your food during lunch.

23:03.181 --> 23:05.684
What about me? I can eat now.

23:06.777 --> 23:08.078
Yours?

23:08.900 --> 23:09.901
I don't have any.

23:15.026 --> 23:16.094
Good luck.

23:47.692 --> 23:48.860
Let's dive in here.

23:52.464 --> 23:53.765
This is different from swimming.

23:54.633 --> 23:56.993
You need to hold your breath in, instead of letting it out.

23:58.837 --> 24:00.172
Holding my breath in?

24:02.574 --> 24:03.808
Then I'll see you down below.

25:11.243 --> 25:13.078
I can't tell anything apart.

25:19.818 --> 25:21.286
Where did you find that?

25:22.287 --> 25:24.122
Did you buy that while I wasn't looking?

25:24.656 --> 25:26.258
Did you forget everything I told you?

25:26.591 --> 25:28.193
I remember everything!

25:28.527 --> 25:29.767
But it's easier said than done.

25:31.396 --> 25:32.464
Put your goggles on.

25:35.534 --> 25:36.568
And then,

25:37.469 --> 25:39.371
- give me your hand. - What?

25:42.140 --> 25:44.376
- Now, breathe in. - Darn it.

26:25.584 --> 26:27.586
When you're underwater, it'll look like this.

26:28.987 --> 26:30.789
This looks like a rock.

26:33.325 --> 26:34.359
Do you see those?

26:36.628 --> 26:38.630
I see. Are those respiratory pores?

26:41.733 --> 26:43.502
Rocks don't have these holes.

26:44.469 --> 26:46.605
When you're underwater, take your time...

26:47.105 --> 26:48.740
to examine the rocks.

26:49.307 --> 26:50.976
Then you'll feel the abalones breathing.

27:52.571 --> 27:55.173
I found one! I caught it!

27:55.974 --> 27:58.376
What? What did you catch?

27:59.244 --> 28:00.245
An abalone!

28:03.515 --> 28:06.084
No way. An abalone?

28:06.685 --> 28:08.587
That's my Parang-ri Mermaid!

28:08.720 --> 28:10.989
Nice job, An Na!

28:15.160 --> 28:16.194
Look!

28:22.901 --> 28:25.303
Don't get too excited or ambitious after catching one.

28:25.470 --> 28:26.905
Do as much as your breath allows.

28:27.405 --> 28:28.607
Stop nagging.

28:30.442 --> 28:33.245
I've been waiting for this day for a long time.

28:33.778 --> 28:34.779
Have some faith in me.

28:35.947 --> 28:37.048
See you down there.

30:18.517 --> 30:20.237
If I continue to wait for the right timing,

30:21.653 --> 30:22.654
will my dream...

30:24.356 --> 30:25.857
ever see the light of day again...

30:27.559 --> 30:28.627
someday?

30:46.444 --> 30:47.679
Are you that happy?

30:48.613 --> 30:50.482
Yes, and I owe it to you.

30:53.118 --> 30:54.186
I feel great.

30:55.554 --> 30:57.856
I take back what I said last time.

31:00.492 --> 31:01.893
That you were rude...

31:02.761 --> 31:04.296
but oddly sweet.

31:05.030 --> 31:06.064
Then what?

31:07.032 --> 31:10.101
You aren't rude, but you aren't sweet, either.

31:12.437 --> 31:14.139
Isn't that worse?

31:14.940 --> 31:16.074
Instead,

31:16.842 --> 31:19.010
you remind me of the sea.

31:23.215 --> 31:25.684
On the surface, you surge with waves and push people away.

31:26.451 --> 31:28.186
But you're deep and peaceful on the inside.

31:30.121 --> 31:33.291
Although I haven't known you for long,

31:34.693 --> 31:36.161
I feel like I can trust you.

31:43.268 --> 31:44.769
You're a bad judge of character.

31:45.804 --> 31:47.706
Jeez, I know you liked it.

31:48.473 --> 31:51.176
Anyway, thank you...

31:55.814 --> 31:58.517
for teaching me how to harvest seafood.

32:38.356 --> 32:40.425
Hey. You.

32:44.029 --> 32:46.698
I heard this guy lives here. Is that right?

32:48.333 --> 32:49.367
Who's that?

32:51.970 --> 32:54.372
Hey, yes. Yoon Duk Hyun!

32:55.140 --> 32:57.308
That's Yoon Duk Hyun!

32:57.309 --> 33:00.345
He lives over there in that house with a red roof.

33:03.215 --> 33:05.851
By the way, why are you...

33:06.685 --> 33:08.086
looking for him?

33:12.724 --> 33:13.825
May I ask why?

33:14.659 --> 33:15.660
Why?

33:18.129 --> 33:19.531
Is he someone I shouldn't look for?

33:21.466 --> 33:24.169
No, it's not that.

33:28.974 --> 33:32.243
It's because he owes me something.

33:32.244 --> 33:33.278
Don't be scared.

33:39.317 --> 33:40.552
What a nice life you have,

33:42.420 --> 33:43.522
Yoon Duk Hyun.
